# Scarborough Fair — traditional English ballad (Child 2 family). Public domain
# (traditional verses only). Shows: Drop D tuning, custom voicings using the low
# D, two strum patterns, slides, a bend and release, repeated section.
{title: Scarborough Fair}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 3/4}
{tuning: Drop D}
{comment: Tab is approximate (written from memory) — the interlude melody is simplified.}

{define: Dm 0 x 0 2 3 1 fingers 0 0 0 2 3 1}
{define: Dsus2 0 x 0 2 3 0 fingers 0 0 0 1 3 0}
{define: G x x 0 0 0 3 fingers 0 0 0 0 0 3}

{strum: waltz = D - D U D U}
{strum: lilt = D - - U D -}

{section: Intro}
{use: lilt x4}
[Dm] [Dsus2] [Dm] [Dm]

{section: Verse 1}
{use: waltz x16}
[Dm]Are you [Dm]going to [C]Scarborough [Dm]Fair?
[Dm]Parsley, [F]sage, rose[G]mary and [Dm]thyme
[Dm]Remember [F]me to [C]one who lives [Dm]there
[C]For she [Dm]once was a [C]true love of [Dm]mine

{section: Verse 2}
{use: waltz x16}
[Dm]Tell her to [Dm]make me a [C]cambric [Dm]shirt
[Dm]Parsley, [F]sage, rose[G]mary and [Dm]thyme
[Dm]Without no [F]seams nor [C]needle[Dm]work
[C]Then she'll [Dm]be a [C]true love of [Dm]mine

{section: Verse 3}
{use: waltz x16}
[Dm]Tell her to [Dm]find me an [C]acre of [Dm]land
[Dm]Parsley, [F]sage, rose[G]mary and [Dm]thyme
[Dm]Between the [F]salt water [C]and the sea [Dm]strand
[C]Then she'll [Dm]be a [C]true love of [Dm]mine

{section: Interlude}
{use: lilt x4}
[Dm] [C] [Dm] [Dm]
{tab}
e|------------|------------|------------|------------|
B|------------|------------|----3b5r3-1-|------------|
G|--------2---|2/4-----4---|2-----------|2---4\2-----|
D|0---0-------|----------3-|------------|--------0---|
A|------------|------------|------------|------------|
D|------------|------------|------------|--------0---|
{end_tab}

{section: Outro}
{use: lilt x2}
[Dsus2] [Dm]
{comment: Let it ring}

{order: Intro, Verse 1, Interlude, Verse 2, Interlude, Verse 3, Outro}
